# finance-tracker-api — Project Context

Single-user personal finance REST API built with ASP.NET Core + EF Core + SQL Server.

## What this project is

- Track income and expense transactions
- Assign categories to transactions
- Generate reports (weekly, monthly, or any date range) with category breakdowns
- Export data as JSON or CSV
- MCP-style context snapshots for deterministic AI-assisted categorization

## What this project is NOT

No authentication, authorization, multi-user support, or frontend UI. Do not add any of these.

## Tech stack

- ASP.NET Core Web API / C#
- Entity Framework Core (SQL Server for local dev, in-memory for tests)
- xUnit + FluentAssertions
- GitHub Actions CI

## Project structure

```
src/Finance.Api/          — API project
tests/Finance.Api.Tests/  — xUnit test project
artifacts/                — agent_log.txt, context_schema.md, example_context_snapshot.json
.github/workflows/ci.yml  — CI pipeline
```

## Core domain entities

- `Transaction` — single income or expense entry
- `Category` — groups transactions (Groceries, Transport, Salary, etc.)
- `Report` — aggregated totals for a given period
- `CategoryBreakdown` — per-category totals within a date range
- `FinanceContextSnapshot` — MCP-style context snapshot

## API conventions

- Route prefix: `/api/`
- Report endpoints accept `from`/`to` query params (ISO 8601 dates), not hardcoded week offsets
- Export endpoints: `GET /api/export/json` and `GET /api/export/csv`

## Testing rules

- Use in-memory EF Core provider in tests — no real DB required
- CI must pass without secrets or local SQL Server
- Cover aggregation boundary edge cases (period start/end, empty periods, single-entry periods)

## Security — never store or expose

Bank account numbers, card numbers, real personal identifiers, API keys, passwords, tokens, or production secrets.

## AI development log

Log every meaningful AI interaction in `artifacts/agent_log.txt` with: timestamp, model, prompt, suggestion, decision (accepted/rejected), and reason.
